codex
The mapper behavior builds, but the new stmap28 diagnostic counter can report penalty seeds when no penalty was applied, making the experiment statistics inaccurate.

Review comment:

- [P2] Only count seeds when a penalty was applied — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:927-929
  In mode 29, low-reference moderate candidates (`nRefs < 5`) still set `fStmap28ModeratePenaltyCandidate`, but `Map_MatchStmap28ModeratePenaltyFactor()` returns `0.0` for them, so they are accepted through the normal one-inverter margin. This block still increments `nStmap28ModeratePenaltySeed` and emits a `penalty seed diag`, which overstates accepted choices that actually exercised the soft penalty (as in the current syn2 run for a refs=4 seed).
